# XCU cxref
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# cxref output format is unspecified beyond the file name line, the sorted
# symbols, the declaring asterisk, the function name and the line numbers;
# the tests find the block of lines that starts at a symbol in the first
# column and look for those pieces in it; a listing laid out otherwise is
# UNRESOLVED, not FAIL.

assertion  XCU.cxref.001
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The listing starts with the input file name on its own line, then
           has an entry for auto, static and global symbols and for macros
           from #define, each giving its line numbers with an asterisk
           before the declaring one and the name of the function it appears
           in.
test       t/001-listing.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.002
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The symbols in the listing are sorted, in the collation sequence
           of the POSIX locale.
test       t/002-sorted.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.003
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -s leaves out the line with the input file name.
test       t/003-silent.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.004
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -o sends the listing to the named file instead of standard
           output.
test       t/004-output-file.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.005
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Without -c each input file has its own portion starting with its
           file name; with -c the files are cross-referenced together in one
           sorted list of symbols.
test       t/005-combined.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.006
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With -w and a number of 51 or more, no output line is wider than
           that many columns even for a symbol with many references.
note       Q-179 in docs/standard-issues.md: only widths of 51 and above are
           tested.
test       t/006-width.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.007
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -D defines and -U removes a macro, the later of the two for a
           name wins, and -I names a directory searched for quoted include
           files.
test       t/007-preprocessor-options.sh

assertion  XCU.cxref.008
anchor     utilities/cxref.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A file operand that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit status.
test       t/008-missing-file.sh
